# 一、§5.3.2 编码器消融（定稿，−0.35 页）

整段替换原来的 "Encoder Choices." 段：

Encoder Choices. Replacing the tabular and time-series encoders of RAN-MP with general-purpose alternatives (TPB-TTMs and TPB-TM, Section 5.1) reduces accuracy on all use cases. On RANPerf, RAN-MP-Core exceeds TPB-TM and TPB-TTMs in AUPRC by 0.176 and 0.207, respectively (Table 2). On EngSav, both variants have higher errors than the baseline (Table 3). On EngCon, they reduce MAPE but incur higher RMSE and percentile errors (Table 4). These results indicate that single-modality, general-purpose encoders are not well suited to RAN profiling. Pretrained models from other domains, such as TTMs, are further limited by the sequence-length constraints of their backbones, which restrict their capacity to represent high-dimensional RAN data, and by their reliance on pretrained word embeddings, which are less effective for configuration features and performance indicators that lack natural-language semantics. In contrast, the lightweight SAINT-based design of RAN-MP imposes no such constraints.

